## What this predicate means

**A `superseded-by` B** — B replaces A in A's role (inverse of `supersedes`).  The author-side admission that A is no longer authoritative; readers should follow B.

A memorial declaring its own supersession is the editorial gesture that keeps the corpus's lifecycle-status consistent without requiring readers to scan B-side declarations.

